# Timing artifacts, not source. run_trial.sh writes logs and per-tick traces
# here; a 309 s two-arm trace is ~6 MB of CSV that a later run rewrites
# wholesale, so versioning them put 60,000-line diffs in the history for data
# that `run_trial.sh -g -d 300 -T data/nmpc_timing/trace.csv` regenerates in five
# minutes. Every number worth keeping is quoted, with its machine state, in the
# root README's realtime section.
#
# This file is tracked so the directory exists in a fresh clone -- the tooling's
# examples write straight into it, and the node's ofstream does not create
# missing directories.
*.csv
*.log
!.gitignore
